{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1795770736,"nonce":"MWb/rceRpXtqToUODyjzv8+nLUA=","title":"cn components ignore an application's shadow variables","message":"cn_bundle().with_css(\":root { --shadow-md: ... }\") leaves cn buttons, inputs and cards on the theme's shadows. Rules in the application's own source see the new value. Rules in the application's own stylesheet that set box-shadow do win over cn, including on hover and focus.\n\nTwo causes. add_css resolves var() in each source as it is added, with the variables known by then, so a later :root override does not reach cn's stylesheet. A colour scheme change reparses all sources together and then it does, so the same app looks different after a toggle. The card also sets its shadow from the theme tokens in Rust, so --shadow-sm never reaches it.\n\nFound checking that the default theme keeps a user's shadows (GitHub #86).","files":null}]}